# Code Modification (The Game Shelf)

Before extending features or moving code across layers, read
`docs/architecture.md` and `docs/development-guide.md`. For game content, also
read `.agents/skills/add-game/SKILL.md` and
`docs/rules-guide-system.md`. For unified rule interactions, read
`.agents/skills/hybrid-interactive-rules/SKILL.md`.

After verification, follow `verify-then-push.mdc`.

## Layers

| Path | Role |
|---|---|
| `content/games/` | Source of truth: `index.json`, `meta.json`, bilingual `rules.md`, optional `score.json`, `trainer.json`, `calculator.json`, `play.json` |
| `src/` | App Router, feature UI, shared layout, domain libraries, shared types |
| `public/data/` | Generated by `prebuild`; never hand-edit |
| `scripts/` | Build-time validation, generation, migration, and postbuild hooks |
| `bbge/` | Playable engine; keep it separate from rules UI |

Static export (`output: "export"`, `basePath: "/boardgames"`, trailing slash)
means no API routes, middleware, or runtime Node features in the app.

## Data loading

- Server pages use `GameRepository` / `GameFactory` and
  `params: Promise<…>`; do not invent another content loader.
- Rules use one `en/rules.md` and one `zh/rules.md`. `GameFactory` parses each
  into `RuleDocument`; `RuleDocumentExperience` renders the shared interaction
  primitives.
- Do not add or restore `flow.json`, `guide.json`, a flow-only route, or a
  second JSON copy of rule prose.
- Client fetches (chat, covers) use `/boardgames/…`; covers use the generated
  `cover-manifest.json`.

## Server vs client

- Keep `src/app/[locale]/**/page.tsx` as Server Components.
- Put stateful UI under `src/features/` or `src/shared/` with a narrow
  `"use client"` boundary.
- Do not move hooks onto an entire page just to support one feature.

## i18n

- UI chrome comes from `messages/en.json` and `messages/zh.json`.
- Game content keeps bilingual fields in `meta.json` and optional feature JSON;
  rule text and interaction structure live separately in `en/rules.md` and
  `zh/rules.md` with matching stable IDs.
- Links use `next/link` and `/${locale}/…/` with trailing slashes.

## Feature wiring

| Feature | Source | Renderer |
|---|---|---|
| Rules + interactions | `en\|zh/rules.md` → `RuleDocument` | `games/[slug]/page.tsx` → `RuleDocumentExperience` |
| Score | `score.json` | `features/score/registry.tsx` |
| Trainer | `trainer.json` | `features/trainer/registry.tsx` + domain library |
| Calculator | `calculator.json` | `features/calculator` |
| Play | `play.json` | `features/play` → `bbge/` |

Shared types belong in `src/types/game.ts` or the relevant domain library. Do
not add `src/lib/content/types.ts` or a parallel feature registry.

## UI and content red lines

- Use existing Tailwind tokens from `src/app/globals.css`; no new palette,
  dark mode, Ant Design, Less, shadcn, axios, Zustand, or empty service/store
  folders.
- Keep `RuleDocumentExperience` generic. Add a parser directive or reusable
  component for a repeated rule shape; do not add slug conditionals for one
  game.
- Keep summaries actionable and visible; use `rule-details` only for optional
  examples and exceptions.
- Preserve full-rule mode, print, export, TOC, metadata, family links, chat,
  keyboard behavior, and no-JavaScript readability.
- Never edit `public/data/` by hand.
